text t_s294 "compile_command_note"
text t_s295 " bytes) holds no compile line for build/gpu_decode_graph_test: make did not rebuild it in this run, so the flags are not recorded; the binary is identified by binary_sha256\""
text t_s296 "\"median over "
text t_s297 " tokens (sorted value at index n/2), each field's median taken on its own, so derived differences are differences of medians\""
text t_s298 "record_ns"
text t_s299 "not written by gpu_decode_graph_test; submit_now() in omega_gpu_decode_graph.c fails the token when sems_done != launches, so a PASS run implies sems_done == launches for every timed token (inferred, not a recorded value)"
text t_s300 "as for graph: not recorded, implied by the PASS verdict"
text t_s301 "identical_to_graph"
text t_s302 "note"
text t_s303 "the same recorded list submitted one launch per submission (TEST ONLY set_flush_each): the batching comparison inside the same run"
text t_s304 "one extra token run with set_stamps(1): span_ns and stage times are device PTIMER differences; chip_ns is that token's host-clock submit span; unattributed_ns = chip_ns - span_ns (submit call, front-end start, completion marker and host poll)"
text t_s305 ""
text t_s306 "available"
text t_s307 "reason"
text t_s308 "the input receipt carries per-token medians and one stamped token only, no per-token arrays or run totals, so no aggregate sums or percentiles are derived (adding them needs the test to write every token's stats)"
text t_s309 "\"serial: the sum over the token's submissions of one host-clock span each ("
text t_s310 " submission per graph token, "
text t_s311 " per flush_each token); spans never overlap each other\""
text t_s312 "\"serial partition with "
text t_s313 " independent launches: prefetch on, each layer's o_proj prefetch is marked independent (no barrier before it) and tagged attn, so its stamp is the front-end time while the attention may still run; the attn stage is the attention+prefetch window and the stages still add up to span_ns\""
text t_s314 "barrier 1 (none, TEST ONLY): no WAIT_FOR_IDLE before the stamps, so a stage time is a front-end interval, not a launch duration"
text t_s315 "\"serial partition: barrier "
text t_s316 ") puts a WAIT_FOR_IDLE before every stamp and prefetch is off, so launches run one after another and the stage times add up exactly to span_ns\""
text t_s317 "overlap_measurable"
text t_s318 "an overlapped window is visible (the attn stage holds attention + prefetch), but no counter splits it, so how much of the two launches overlapped is not measurable from these counters"
text t_s319 "every launch waits for the previous one (WFI) and the host records before it submits, so nothing overlaps to measure; device time inside the host span is span_ns, the rest is unattributed_ns"
text t_s320 "device_clock"
text t_s321 "GPU PTIMER ns from compute-class REPORT_SEMAPHORE timestamps (omega_gpu_cmdlist.h: \"out[0] = GPU timestamp (ns, PTIMER) before launch 0, out[i + 1] = after launch i completed (taken after its WAIT_FOR_IDLE)\"); used only by stamped_token span_ns and stages"
text t_s322 "host_clock"
text t_s323 "omega_gpu_session_now_ns(): the platform's time_now_ns, CLOCK_MONOTONIC on Linux (omega_gpu_platform_linux.c ref_now_ns); used by chip_ns, record_ns and total_ns"
text t_s324 "counters"
text t_s325 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"launches recorded for the token\""
text t_s326 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"submissions (1 normally; = launches with flush_each)\""
text t_s327 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"sum of the list submissions' first-submit-to-last-marker time\". HOST clock, not device time: omega_gpu_cmdlist_submit() reads time_now_ns just before queue_submit and again after both completion marker words were seen and synced, so it holds device execution plus submit, fetch and poll latency"
text t_s328 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"host: begin_token to the submit (recording)\""
text t_s329 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"host: begin_token to end_token return\""
text t_s330 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"launch semaphores found DONE\""
text t_s331 "stamps"
text t_s332 "omega_gpu_decode_graph.h: \"Launch i took stamps[i + 1] - stamps[i] ns\"; gpu_decode_graph_test sums them per kind (per_kind_ns)"
text t_s333 "derived: total_ns - chip_ns, both host clock: recording, attention counter check, output sync, token read and lock, everything outside the submit span"
text t_s334 "numbers copied from the stats file written by tests/gpu_decode_graph_test.c --out; settings from its log; identity from the runner's device.txt and binaries.sha256"
text t_s335 "chip_ns is host-clock time around the device work; the only device-clock numbers are the stamped token's span_ns and stages"
text t_s336 "per-token values are independent medians of a synthetic step on random weights (Qwen3-30B-A3B shapes, not a checkpoint), one fixed position, the same token every rep; not a serving or end-to-end tokens-per-second figure"
text t_s337 "the stamped token is a single token: its stage times are one sample, not a distribution"
text t_s338 "sems_done, the command list's own host_ns (method-stream build) and the marker-wait part of chip_ns are not recorded per token"
text t_s339 "no aggregate totals or percentiles: the input has medians only"
text t_s340 "this receipt is not a qualification: it re-expresses an existing run and claims nothing beyond that run's files"
text t_s341 "the run's tree was dirty: the commit alone does not reproduce the binary; see worktree.diff in the run directory when present"
